invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh rsa-addcarry
reason: a gcc build for x86-64 no longer runs rsa_mont64_addcarry.c's rows
  and runs the loops, whose every word waits on the carry of the word
  below. The words are the same, so no equivalence test sees it. The lane
  compiles rsa_mont64.c with gcc for x86-64 and requires that it call
  both row entries. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
#if defined(__x86_64__) && defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)
#define RSA_MONT64_ADDCARRY 1
--- new
#if defined(__x86_64__) && defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)
#define RSA_MONT64_ADDCARRY 0
